                                    <a class="collapsed" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse4th" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse4th"><span class="color-dark-grey">Citrus-Rosemary Turkey Brine</span></a>
                                </h2>
                            </div>
                            <div id="collapse4th" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingFour">
                                <div class="panel-body p-5">
                                <div class="wrapper-account-banner"><picture> <source media="(min-width: 768px)" srcset="/images/content/how-to-turkey-brine-citrus-turkey-brine.jpg" /> <source media="(min-width: 320px)" srcset="/images/content/how-to-turkey-brine-citrus-turkey-brine.jpg" /><img alt="citrus turkey brine recipe" class="w-100" src="/images/content/how-to-turkey-brine-citrus-turkey-brine.jpg" /> </picture></div><br>
<p class="roboto color-dark-grey text-center"><strong>Prep Time</strong>: 5 Minutes</p>
<p class="roboto color-dark-grey text-center"><strong>Cook Time</strong>: 15 Minutes</p>

	<h4 class="roboto color-dark-grey">Ingredients</h4>
<ul class="roboto color-dark-grey">
<li>1 gallon low/no-sodium vegetable broth</li>
<li>1 gallon ice water</li>
<li>1 1/2 cup coarse kosher salt (3/4 cup, if using table salt)</li>
<li>1/4 cup granulated sugar</li>
<li>3 oranges, quartered </li>
<li>6 cloves garlic, smashed</li>
<li>8 sprigs rosemary</li>
<li>6 bay leaves </li></ul>
<h4 class="roboto color-dark-grey">Instructions</h4>
<p class="roboto color-dark-grey">Bring all ingredients, minus the ice water, to a boil in a large stock pot.  Make sure that sugar and salt are completely dissolved, and remove from heat.  Add the ice water to the hot brine.  Once cooled, add turkey, and refrigerate for 12 to 24 hours before cooking.  When ready to cook, remove turkey from brine and pat dry. </p>
